entry electromagnetic-radiation
term: Electromagnetic Radiation
related_terms: gamma-ray
related_terms: radiation
related_terms: gamma-radiation
related_terms: ionizing-radiation
quick_facts: Light is electromagnetic radiation
quick_facts: Gamma rays are electromagnetic radiation too
quick_facts: It is energy, not matter
quick_facts: Different kinds carry different amounts of energy
quick_facts: Alpha and beta are particles, not electromagnetic radiation

sources:
    {"organization":"OpenStax","title":"University Physics Volume 2: Electromagnetic Waves","url":"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/16-introduction"}

definition:
    Energy that travels as waves of electric and magnetic fields. It is not made of matter. Radio waves, microwaves, infrared, visible light, ultraviolet, X-rays and gamma rays are all electromagnetic radiation. They differ in how much energy they carry. Gamma rays carry far more energy than visible light.

debunking_snippet:
    “Radiation always means nuclear radiation.” Light is radiation too. Only some radiation comes from nuclei.
